  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="9254-4912-74e6-b71a" name="Wars of the Roses English (Armies of Chivalry) - List Notes" publicationId="da79-edc9-ea11-dbc4" hidden="false">
      <description>WARS OF THE ROSES ENGLISH 1455-1487 (Armies of Chivalry, pp.62-63). Five army compositions: Lancaster, York, Richard III, Henry Tudor and the Yorkist Pretenders; availability of some troop types is restricted to specific armies. Mixed Order: Retinue Longbowmen - Dismounted Men-at-Arms; Retinue Longbowmen - Retinue Billmen; Shire Longbowmen - Shire Billmen or Border Spearmen; Welsh Longbowmen - Welsh Spearmen; Continental Mercenaries (melee weapons) - Continental Mercenaries (missile weapons).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Wars of the Roses English - Lancaster]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-50%, Infantry 25-75%, Special Units 0-25%.
[Wars of the Roses English - York]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-50%, Infantry 25-75%, Special Units 0-25%.
[Wars of the Roses English - Richard III]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-50%, Infantry 25-75%, Special Units 0-25%.
[Wars of the Roses English - Henry Tudor]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Infantry: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-50%, Infantry 25-75%, Special Units 0-25%.
[Wars of the Roses English - Yorkist Pretenders]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 25%
  Special Units: up to 75%, at least 25%
  Characters 0-25%, Cavalry 0-25%, Infantry 0-25%, Special Units 25-75%.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
